carlos-ctl (1.2.2~dev1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Fix OSCAR 19 collation aliases and note-lock classification. Compare
    converted text exactly, including trailing spaces, and use target
    comparison rules for source keys and merge mappings.
  * Support complete SQL backup sets and native nested OSCAR archives,
    verify overlaps, and restore ordered full/incremental document sets.
    Bind private input snapshots and the ETL contract to resume state.
  * Guard acknowledged charset repairs before speculative conversions,
    preserving correct accents and supplementary Unicode without warnings.
  * Refuse conversion warnings and value mismatches before checkpoints.
    Verify the packaged physical schema, all declared foreign keys and
    optimizer statistics before completing an import.
  * Retire source-set provenance and diagnostics with the completed run,
    and remove its immutable raw input copies during verified cleanup.
  * Explain an active import immediately in deployment checks.

